{{also|hacke|hacké}}
==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhakə/|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gml|de}} {{m|gml|hakke}}. Also {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|hakka||animal heel}}, which has no attested continuation in [[w:Middle High German|Middle High German]], however. Compare {{cog|nl|hak}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Hacken}}

# {{lb|de|regional|chiefly|northern and central Germany}} [[heel]] (of the foot)
# {{lb|de|regional|chiefly|northern and central Germany}} the back of the [[shoe]], which is around the [[heel]] (including or excluding the [[sole]], for which alone {{m|de|Absatz}} is used)

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|de|Ferse}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|hacke}}. Pertaining to {{m|de|hacken||to chop}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Hacken}}

# [[hoe]]

